ern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f57ec630e3f51d7902083d7b452bfaf33433f7ba.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f57ec630e3f51d7902083d7b452bfaf33433f7ba.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 3:01AM MDT until October 23 at 11:00AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southern Mineral County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1100 AM MDT Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Numerous roads\nremain closed due to flooding.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 300 AM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain. Flooding is\nalready occurring in the warned area. Between 2 and 4 inches of\nrain have fallen.\n- Additional rainfall amounts up to 0.3 inches  are possible in the\nwarned area.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nWolf Creek Pass.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T11:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f04c19ca920a76048140182383c028d090a7e844.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f04c19ca920a76048140182383c028d090a7e844.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 22 at 10:07PM MDT until October 23 at 11:00AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southwestern Saguache County in central Colorado...\nMineral County in south central Colorado...\nRio Grande County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1100 AM MDT Friday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Several structures are flooded and sand bagging\noperations are continuing. Evacuations are occuring from Wolf Creek\nRanch to Fun Valley. Some roads remain closed due to flooding\nin